<title>USA: Showers moisten soil in W Africa cocoa areas - WSC.</title>
<headline>Showers moisten soil in W Africa cocoa areas - WSC.</headline>
<text>
<p>LEXINGTON, MASS.,Feb 27 Reuter) - Scattered showers and thunderstorms are improving soil moisture conditions through key cocoa crop areas of West Africa, forecaster Weather Services Corp said.</p>
<p>Widely scattered to scattered light to moderate showers, with 15-25 percent coverage, mainly in the south, are forecast. Isolated heavier showers are expected Thursday and Friday and temperatures are seen mostly near normal.</p>
<p>The outlook is for little change Saturday-Monday.</p>
</text>
